; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR LUNAR LANDER  -  land gently on the pad   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot, press E (Easy) or H (Hard). Gravity pulls the lander down; the
; up arrow fires the main engine, <- and -> the side thrusters - one burst per press
; (hold a key to repeat), each costing fuel. Land with all three columns on the '='
; pad, falling slowly and hardly drifting. After each game E or H flies again; ESC
; quits.
;          HARD                         EASY
;   gravity every frame          every other frame (half)
;   bursts 5 up / 3 sideways     3 up / 2 sideways
;   fuel 250                     400
;   safe down 20, sideways 8     25, sideways 16
;   pad 7 wide                   11 wide
;
; VT100: cursor addressing, erase to end of line, hide/show cursor. No scrolling.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/lander_verify.py, V0061.34): an autopilot that reads the lander's registers and presses the keys: HARD - lands on two moons (vy 8-9); a pilot coming in at ~26 crashes; lined up over the pad, engine off from 12 rows -> crashes ON the pad at vy 44. EASY - lands on two moons with the 11-wide pad (vy 10-11); engine off from 14 rows still crashes ON the pad at vy 32. Both: the chosen table is the one in use and its name is on the status line; the ground drawn is exactly the height/pad tables; every frame the lander is drawn whole with no copy left; only E or H starts (an arrow does not); hands off it crashes where it comes down; a lone ESC quits cleanly; a rerun without reloading lands again.
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-09-25: Easy "works BEAUTIFULLY". (The
; first, Hard-only version worked but was too hard to land softly - hence Easy.)
;
; 476 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 4005 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: the index for patching strings
; D 4009 11 0E 06 94    LOADXI R14 0694
; D 400D C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; SEED:
; D 400F C3             RAND                               Spin the generator until a key comes: every moon differs
; D 4010 CC             SERST
; D 4011 A1 00 0F       IFFALSEI SEED
; D 4014 BD 04 BD       CALL CHOOSE                        E or H (an ESC on its own quits)
; NEW:
; D 4017 11 0E 06 85    LOADXI R14 0685
; D 401B C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       Clear, hide the cursor
; D 401D 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000
; D 4021 11 07 00 15    LOADXI R7 0015                     the ground starts at row 21
; HG:
; D 4025 C3             RAND                               one step of the random walk per column
; D 4026 21 09          COPYAX Acc -> R9
; D 4028 11 0A 00 03    LOADXI R10 0003
; D 402C 4D 9A          DIVXY R9 / R10
